  (descr "TI BQ25792RQMR, WQFN-29 4x4mm 0.4mm pitch. Real perimeter pad coordinates cross-checked against an independent open-source KiCad footprint for the same part (see docs/BQ25792_VERIFICATION.md). The exposed thermal/ground pad (EP) below is a DOCUMENTED ASSUMPTION -- the reference footprint that supplied the perimeter pad coordinates did not include one, but WQFN packages in this TI family normally have a large center EP; a conservative 1.8x1.4mm EP is added here rather than omitted, since omitting a real EP would be the worse error for a 5A charger IC. Sized specifically to keep >=0.2mm clearance to every perimeter pad (a first pass at 2.4x2.4mm was found, by real KiCad DRC, to touch the bottom-row pads with 0.0mm clearance -- this smaller size is verified clearance-clean but is almost certainly smaller than the real EP, which is normally sized to nearly the full pitch envelope between pad rows. VERIFY EP size against the TI mechanical drawing before fabrication.")
